	(text "Label Convention:\n\nINT			-	Isolated Internal signal or enable that is \n				manipulated/read only on the PCB. Would generally \n				be on the 3.3V side of the circuit.\n\nEXT			-	Non-Isolated External signal or enable that is \n				manipulated/read on the field side. Would generally \n				be on the 24V side of the circuit.\n\nStatus Signal -	Binary (High/Low) signal entering into the \n				microprocessor/PCB/ext.\n\n					example - light lens has 24v going through all light \n					lens and if they are all good then a 24 v signal goes \n					back to microprocessor as an input. Hence the name \n					\"LIGHT LENS STATUS\"\n\nSignal		-	Continuous (analog/pwm/ext.) signal entering into the \n				microprocessor/PCB/ext.\n\n					example - Pressure transmitter is being read by the \n					microprocessor and can read pressure from 0 to 1\" \n					watercolumn. Hence the name \n					\"PRESSURE TRANSMITTER SIGNAL\"\n\nGNDA		-	Analog Ground. attached to the negative end of the 24vdc \n				power supply feeding out timer board.\n\nGNDD		-	Digital Ground. attached to the negative end of the 3.3vdc \n				power supply feeding our 3.3v side of the timer board.\n\nGNDS		-	Signal Ground. attached to the Ground end of the MODBUS/ \n				I2C/Whatever Protocall we use to communicater to other \n				timer boiards.\n\nEnable - 		signal exiting the microprocessor\n\n					example - VFD RUN signal is sent out of the microprocessor\n					which goes to the mosfet which send signal to vfd to \n					run. Hence the name \n					\"VFD RUN ENABLE\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3b3d7c22-e70d-4e47-9dee-89fa88f68f53")
	)
